## 1. Executive Summary

LipiScript is a SaaS platform that converts handwritten notes into editable digital text and professionally formatted e-books.

The primary feasibility question is whether available OCR and vision-language models can reliably recognize handwritten Marathi, Hindi, English, and mixed-language content while preserving the original meaning and script.

The system must:

- Convert handwritten notes into editable digital text.
- Support Marathi, Hindi, English, and mixed-language pages with equal importance.
- Preserve the original language and wording.
- Never automatically correct spelling, grammar, punctuation, or rewrite content.
- Mark uncertain or unreadable words as `[illegible]` rather than guessing.
- Allow users to manually edit the transcribed content.
- Generate a clean, professional PDF with headings, paragraphs, bullets, a simple cover, chapter-wise table of contents, and automatic page numbers.
- Keep every user's notes private to that individual account.

**No OCR provider or production architecture is selected in this phase.** The final selection must be based on measured benchmark results, operational requirements, privacy terms, and cost.

### Product guardrails

| Area | Confirmed requirement |
|---|---|
| Languages | Marathi, Hindi, English, mixed-language |
| Uploads | Images, PDFs, camera capture |
| Output | Editable digital text and professional PDF |
| Editing | Manual editing by the user |
| AI correction | Not permitted automatically |
| Unreadable content | Mark as `[illegible]` |
| Privacy | Each user can access only their own notes |
| Sharing | No shared workspaces or team access |
| Formatting | Essential professional formatting only |
| Diagrams | User chooses handling per project |
| Pricing | To be decided later |

